$WW,1$$FG,5,0$ZealOS Full C/C++/Go Toolchain Plan$FG$

$FG,2$Goal:$FG$ Full C/C++ compiler (LLVM/Clang) + Go language support

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
$FG,5$PHASE A: BUILD INFRASTRUCTURE$FG$
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

These tools are required to run configure scripts and build systems.

$FG,2$A1. Shell Interpreter (sh)$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Required features:
  • Variable expansion ($VAR, ${VAR}, ${VAR:-default})
  • Command substitution ($(cmd) and `cmd`)
  • Pipes (cmd1 | cmd2 | cmd3)
  • Redirects (>, >>, <, 2>&1, &>)
  • Control flow (if/then/else/fi, for/do/done, while, case)
  • Functions
  • Background jobs (&)
  • Exit status ($?)
  • Here documents (<<EOF)
  • Quoting ('single', "double", \escape)
  • Glob expansion (*, ?, [abc])

Files: sh.ZC (~3000-5000 lines)

$FG,2$A2. Build Tools$FG$
────────────────────────────────
make    - GNU Make compatible
          • Makefile parsing
          • Variable expansion
          • Pattern rules (%.o: %.c)
          • Automatic variables ($@, $<, $^)
          • Dependency tracking
          • Parallel builds (-j)
          Files: make.ZC (~2000-3000 lines)

install - Install files with permissions
          Files: install.ZC (~200 lines)

cmake   - Minimal CMake (or cmake wrapper)
          Note: May need to cross-compile CMake first
          Alternative: Port ninja build system (simpler)

$FG,2$A3. Additional Text Tools$FG$
────────────────────────────────
sed     - Stream editor
          • s/pattern/replacement/flags
          • Address ranges (1,10 or /pattern/)
          • Commands: d, p, a, i, c, y
          • Hold space (h, H, g, G, x)
          • Branches (b, t)
          Files: sed.ZC (~1500-2000 lines)

awk     - Pattern scanning
          • Field splitting ($1, $2, NF, NR)
          • Pattern { action } rules
          • BEGIN/END blocks
          • Variables and arrays
          • Built-in functions (substr, split, gsub)
          • Printf formatting
          Files: awk.ZC (~2500-3500 lines)

find    - Find files
          • -name, -type, -size, -mtime
          • -exec, -print, -print0
          • Logical operators (-a, -o, !)
          Files: find.ZC (~800-1000 lines)

xargs   - Build command lines
          • -0 (null delimiter)
          • -n (max args)
          • -P (parallel)
          • -I {} (replacement)
          Files: xargs.ZC (~400-600 lines)

$FG,2$A4. Compression Tools$FG$
────────────────────────────────
gzip    - DEFLATE compression
          • Compress/decompress
          • -c (stdout), -d (decompress), -k (keep)
          Files: gzip.ZC + deflate.ZC (~2000-3000 lines)

tar     - Archive tool
          • Create (-c), extract (-x), list (-t)
          • Compression (-z gzip, -j bzip2)
          • -f file, -v verbose
          • Handle tar headers
          Files: tar.ZC (~1500-2000 lines)

bzip2   - BWT compression (optional, but common)
          Files: bzip2.ZC (~1500 lines)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
$FG,5$PHASE B: COMPLETE LIBC + SYSTEM LIBRARIES$FG$
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

$FG,2$B1. Threading (pthreads)$FG$
────────────────────────────────
pthread_create, pthread_join, pthread_exit
pthread_mutex_init/lock/unlock/destroy
pthread_cond_init/wait/signal/broadcast
pthread_rwlock_*
pthread_key_create (thread-local storage)
pthread_once
pthread_attr_*

Implementation: Map to ZealOS task system
Files: pthread.ZC (~1000-1500 lines)

$FG,2$B2. Memory Mapping$FG$
────────────────────────────────
mmap    - Map files/anonymous memory
munmap  - Unmap
mprotect - Change protection
msync   - Sync to disk

Implementation: Requires kernel support or emulation
Files: mmap.ZC (~500-800 lines)

$FG,2$B3. Signals$FG$
────────────────────────────────
signal, sigaction
sigprocmask, sigsuspend
kill, raise
sigset operations

Implementation: ZealOS doesn't have Unix signals
               Need emulation layer
Files: signal.ZC (~800-1000 lines)

$FG,2$B4. Process Management$FG$
────────────────────────────────
fork    - Create process (challenging in ZealOS)
exec*   - Execute program
wait*   - Wait for child
pipe    - Create pipe
dup/dup2 - Duplicate file descriptors

Implementation: May need to redesign for ZealOS model
Files: process.ZC (~1000-1500 lines)

$FG,2$B5. Networking (already have basics)$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Verify complete:
  socket, bind, listen, accept, connect
  send, recv, sendto, recvfrom
  select, poll
  getaddrinfo, getnameinfo
  setsockopt, getsockopt

$FG,2$B6. Math Library (libm)$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Trigonometric: sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan, atan2
Hyperbolic: sinh, cosh, tanh, asinh, acosh, atanh
Exponential: exp, exp2, expm1, log, log2, log10, log1p
Power: pow, sqrt, cbrt, hypot
Rounding: ceil, floor, trunc, round, nearbyint
Remainder: fmod, remainder, remquo
Floating: frexp, ldexp, modf, scalbn, copysign
Comparison: fmax, fmin, fdim, fabs
Classification: fpclassify, isnan, isinf, isfinite
Error/Gamma: erf, erfc, lgamma, tgamma

Implementation: Software implementations or x87 FPU
Files: libm.ZC (~2000-3000 lines)

$FG,2$B7. Dynamic Linker$FG$
────────────────────────────────
If we want shared libraries (.so):
  • ELF parser
  • Symbol resolution
  • Relocation processing
  • PLT/GOT setup

Alternative: Static linking only (simpler)
Files: ld.so.ZC (~3000-5000 lines if implemented)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
$FG,5$PHASE C: LLVM/CLANG PORT$FG$
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

$FG,2$C1. Create ZealOS Target in LLVM$FG$
────────────────────────────────
LLVM needs a "target triple" for ZealOS:
  x86_64-unknown-zealos

Required components:
  • Target info (data layout, pointer size)
  • Calling convention (use SysV AMD64 ABI)
  • Object file format (ELF or custom)
  • Relocation types
  • System headers location

Files to create in LLVM source:
  llvm/lib/Target/X86/X86TargetZealOS.cpp
  clang/lib/Basic/Targets/ZealOS.h
  clang/lib/Basic/Targets/ZealOS.cpp
  clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/ZealOS.h
  clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/ZealOS.cpp

$FG,2$C2. Cross-Compile LLVM$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Build on Linux:
  cmake -DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING=True \
        -DLLVM_TARGET_ARCH=X86 \
        -DLLVM_DEFAULT_TARGET_TRIPLE=x86_64-unknown-zealos \
        -DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=X86 \
        ...

This produces clang/clang++ that outputs ZealOS binaries.

$FG,2$C3. Port to Native$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Once we have cross-compiled clang:
  1. Build LLVM on ZealOS using cross-compiled clang
  2. Now we have native clang on ZealOS
  3. Self-hosting achieved

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
$FG,5$PHASE D: GO LANGUAGE PORT$FG$
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

$FG,2$D1. Port Go 1.4$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Go 1.4 is the last version written in C.
Source: https://go.dev/dl/go1.4-bootstrap-20171003.tar.gz

Required:
  • Working C compiler (clang from Phase C)
  • Complete libc with pthreads
  • mmap support
  • Signals (or emulation)

Build:
  cd go/src
  ./make.bash

$FG,2$D2. Go Runtime Requirements$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Go runtime needs:
  • Goroutine scheduler (m:n threading)
  • Garbage collector
  • Stack management (segmented/copying stacks)
  • System calls for:
    - Memory (mmap, madvise)
    - Threading (clone/futex on Linux → adapt for ZealOS)
    - Time (clock_gettime)
    - Networking (epoll → adapt to ZealOS)
    - Signals (for preemption)

Files to modify in Go:
  src/runtime/os_zealos.go      (new)
  src/runtime/sys_zealos_amd64.s (new)
  src/syscall/syscall_zealos.go (new)
  src/syscall/zsyscall_zealos_amd64.go (new)

$FG,2$D3. Bootstrap Modern Go$FG$
────────────────────────────────
Once Go 1.4 works:
  GOROOT_BOOTSTRAP=/path/to/go1.4 ./make.bash

This builds Go 1.20+ using Go 1.4.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
$FG,5$ESTIMATED EFFORT$FG$
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Phase A (Build Infrastructure):     ~15,000-20,000 lines
Phase B (Complete libc):            ~10,000-15,000 lines
Phase C (LLVM port):                ~2,000-5,000 lines (ZealOS-specific)
                                    + configuration/build work
Phase D (Go port):                  ~5,000-10,000 lines (ZealOS-specific)

Total new ZealOS code:              ~35,000-50,000 lines

Timeline estimate:
  Phase A: 2-4 weeks
  Phase B: 2-3 weeks
  Phase C: 2-4 weeks (mostly configuration)
  Phase D: 2-4 weeks

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
$FG,5$ALTERNATIVE: SIMPLER GO PORT$FG$
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Instead of full LLVM, we could:

1. Use TCC for C compilation (limited but works)
2. Cross-compile Go on Linux targeting ZealOS
3. Only need ZealOS runtime support, not full toolchain

This is faster but means:
  • No native C++ on ZealOS
  • No building Go from source on ZealOS
  • Dependency on Linux for toolchain

